1
00:00:14,702 --> 00:00:26,742
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,238 --> 00:02:08,238
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

3
00:02:10,470 --> 00:02:11,760
I have a question.

4
00:02:12,609 --> 00:02:16,479
What’s going to happen to this world...

5
00:02:17,941 --> 00:02:20,221
...while we try to keep our own lands
safe?

6
00:02:22,058 --> 00:02:23,578
Everything is devestated.

7
00:02:25,535 --> 00:02:26,735
Diseases.

8
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:29,630
Economic depressions.

9
00:02:30,799 --> 00:02:32,099
Political reckonings.

10
00:02:34,055 --> 00:02:35,325
People are restless.

11
00:02:36,563 --> 00:02:37,723
Fearful and sad.

12
00:02:39,562 --> 00:02:44,342
The army of justice did not show as much
struggle and courage...

13
00:02:44,342 --> 00:02:47,362
... as the sons of the Devil.

14
00:02:49,384 --> 00:02:52,264
The army of justice is conflicted.

15
00:02:53,069 --> 00:02:54,909
And lost its sincerity.

16
00:02:56,670 --> 00:03:00,670
The sons of Devil who found the lands
unprotected...

17
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:04,150
...has begun to attack to end humanity.

18
00:03:05,306 --> 00:03:06,756
But...

19
00:03:06,756 --> 00:03:08,876
...now the fire of justice...

20
00:03:08,876 --> 00:03:10,886
...is lit again.

21
00:03:12,201 --> 00:03:15,451
Our flags will flap...

22
00:03:16,631 --> 00:03:19,391
...and world will find peace once again.

23
00:03:22,705 --> 00:03:30,495
With the help of Allah, our people are
going to destroy the army of Devil.

24
00:03:59,712 --> 00:04:04,762
It means we have already lost the war, if
we post our defending units in the Tent.

25
00:04:05,374 --> 00:04:08,544
Our Alps will hold the surrounding four
hills.

26
00:04:09,259 --> 00:04:15,759
In case of a sudden attack, our Alps will
go through the forest from the stream bed.

27
00:04:15,759 --> 00:04:17,009
And help the Tent.

28
00:04:18,196 --> 00:04:20,486
As you command, Gündüz Bey.

29
00:04:29,196 --> 00:04:31,176
How is the situation in Söğüt, Bamsı Bey?

30
00:04:31,176 --> 00:04:35,346
My Gündüz Bey, as you ordered, I have
engarrisoned Alps near Söğüt.

31
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,590
They are prepared for Balgay’s raid.

32
00:04:38,906 --> 00:04:39,966
Thanks, Bamsı Bey.

33
00:04:47,705 --> 00:04:48,735
At the top...

34
00:04:48,735 --> 00:04:52,525
At the top of Crane and Hawk Hills,
we also engarrisoned Alps.

35
00:04:52,883 --> 00:04:58,393
We will have no mercy on whoever
tries to come to Söğüt.

36
00:04:58,930 --> 00:05:00,280
Thanks, Bamsı Bey.

37
00:05:01,669 --> 00:05:03,719
By the way, Gündüz Bey...

38
00:05:04,059 --> 00:05:07,179
…If Abdurrahman Ghazi already brought
Dündar Bey...

39
00:05:07,179 --> 00:05:09,789
...we should start performing the
funeral prayer.

40
00:05:10,005 --> 00:05:12,395
Abruhhaman Ghazi has not come yet,
Bamsı Bey.

41
00:05:12,834 --> 00:05:14,824
What are you saying, Gündüz Bey?

42
00:05:15,331 --> 00:05:17,741
He must have been here by now.

43
00:05:17,741 --> 00:05:19,771
What if something happened to them?

44
00:05:20,175 --> 00:05:21,735
I will go and ask the Alps.

45
00:05:25,884 --> 00:05:26,674
My Bey...

46
00:05:26,851 --> 00:05:29,861
...Alişar Bey is approaching to Tent
with Seljuk soldiers.

47
00:05:38,501 --> 00:05:41,391
Only that dog’s head will get out of here.

48
00:05:50,102 --> 00:05:51,632
My Batur.

49
00:05:54,152 --> 00:05:57,052
Don’t leave me behind, my son.

50
00:05:58,169 --> 00:05:59,979
Don’t leave, my lovely child.

51
00:06:01,349 --> 00:06:03,349
Don’t leave me, my child.

52
00:06:03,349 --> 00:06:05,279
Take me with you…

53
00:06:05,279 --> 00:06:06,979
…take me with you, my son.

54
00:06:08,221 --> 00:06:11,561
If Batur Brother had known that you
went to Mongols…

55
00:06:11,561 --> 00:06:13,821
…asked for help from Balgay…

56
00:06:14,267 --> 00:06:16,347
...would he even look at your face?

57
00:06:16,347 --> 00:06:17,767
What would he say?

58
00:06:18,517 --> 00:06:19,787
Shut up.

59
00:06:20,949 --> 00:06:24,009
No, I will not shut up.

60
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,623
If you did not use Gündüz Bey as your toy…

61
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:31,330
…my brother would have been still alive.

62
00:06:32,686 --> 00:06:35,836
My brother died because of you.

63
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,940
Because of you.

64
00:06:40,764 --> 00:06:44,364
Even if you make me hush now,
what is going to change?

65
00:06:45,106 --> 00:06:45,856
Shut up!

66
00:06:46,375 --> 00:06:47,175
Shut up!

67
00:06:48,249 --> 00:06:49,569
I said shut up!

68
00:06:49,569 --> 00:06:51,789
Begone now!

69
00:07:19,148 --> 00:07:24,928
I will make all of them pay for what they
did to us, my son.

70
00:07:28,397 --> 00:07:31,047
If I am responsible for your death…

71
00:07:31,047 --> 00:07:32,691
…may Allah take my life away.

72
00:07:35,218 --> 00:07:41,118
I swear that I will take your revenge.

73
00:07:43,966 --> 00:07:49,476
May dying be haram for me before I make
Osman regret the day he was born.

74
00:07:51,141 --> 00:07:52,851
May it be haram, my son.

75
00:07:55,876 --> 00:07:57,316
May it be haram.

76
00:08:27,308 --> 00:08:30,088
I came to your Tent as a Bannerlord,
Gündüz Bey.

77
00:08:38,725 --> 00:08:40,925
The person who killed my Alps…

78
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:44,400
…who made me get hit by an arrow.

79
00:08:49,825 --> 00:08:50,795
Gündüz Bey!

80
00:08:52,107 --> 00:08:53,067
Gündüz Bey!

81
00:08:56,511 --> 00:09:00,291
Aren’t you that person, Alişar Bey?

82
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:11,439
Do you want me to show respect while
you stand in front of me...

83
00:09:11,439 --> 00:09:15,439
... with a Mongol edict that
I don’t care about.

84
00:09:29,518 --> 00:09:31,288
Alişar Bey!

85
00:09:35,050 --> 00:09:39,840
This peltry once belonged
to Ertugrul Ghazi.

86
00:09:41,212 --> 00:09:46,552
Letting somebody who cooperates with
Mongols sit on it does not suit us.

87
00:10:31,482 --> 00:10:32,942
Oh, Allah!

88
00:10:33,927 --> 00:10:39,287
In order to glorify your name,
I'm going towards my path with your name.

89
00:10:41,443 --> 00:10:46,453
My head which raises against the tyrants,
will be only bowed for you.

90
00:10:47,693 --> 00:10:50,503
I expect my desires to
happen only in your way.

91
00:10:51,712 --> 00:10:59,652
Oh almighty, please help me with my war
against the heathens.

92
00:11:01,067 --> 00:11:03,357
Don’t let me go away from your path.

93
00:11:03,985 --> 00:11:08,505
Don’t mistake me with those ill-fated
heathens who run after reputation and fame.

94
00:11:10,609 --> 00:11:15,229
Let me and my people be powerful and wise.

95
00:11:17,122 --> 00:11:20,432
Let he who hears our name
feel safe and secure.

96
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:26,257
Let the tyrants who hear
our prayers be destroyed.

97
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,380
Amin.

98
00:11:34,277 --> 00:11:35,957
Cruelty will end sooner or later.

99
00:11:36,642 --> 00:11:39,912
The era is about to give birth
to a new resurrection...

100
00:11:39,912 --> 00:11:41,832
...as long as you are awake.

101
00:11:42,791 --> 00:11:44,861
As long as you are awake, son.

102
00:11:46,566 --> 00:11:50,566
Whatever happens to Oguz only
happens while he is asleep.

103
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,880
Wake up, son.

104
00:11:57,055 --> 00:12:00,005
Rise, son!

105
00:12:05,854 --> 00:12:08,444
Let the justice walk when you walk.

106
00:12:08,856 --> 00:12:11,986
Let the mercy smile when you smile.

107
00:12:12,086 --> 00:12:16,516
Let the patience stand with you when you
resist against all the cruelties.

108
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:20,590
And let the people see the state in you.

109
00:12:23,763 --> 00:12:26,903
That state should be such a state that...

110
00:12:27,908 --> 00:12:33,798
... justice must be awakened with it and
the world of Islam must find comfort.

111
00:12:34,474 --> 00:12:37,484
Tyrants must quiver with fear...

112
00:12:38,155 --> 00:12:42,155
…and morals should rise once again.

113
00:12:44,094 --> 00:12:48,454
But now the fire of justice is lit.

114
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:56,180
Our flags will flap, and the
world will retrieve peace once again.

115
00:12:57,158 --> 00:13:04,998
With the help of Allah, our people
will destroy the army of Devil.

116
00:13:14,429 --> 00:13:20,519
I came here as the person in charge of the
edict of almighty Mongol ruler, Geyhatu.

117
00:13:21,295 --> 00:13:23,835
Both as a bannerlord…

118
00:13:24,139 --> 00:13:28,649
…and a brother who knows
about all of the Tents.

119
00:13:31,334 --> 00:13:35,534
We don’t have a brother who works
with the cruelties of Mongols.

120
00:13:36,501 --> 00:13:38,711
When it comes to your Bannerlordship...

121
00:13:39,699 --> 00:13:43,699
…as long as you are fair you will
face no trouble coming from us.

122
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,353
What’s your duty here?

123
00:14:03,677 --> 00:14:06,917
Let’s talk outside as
calm as we are able to.

124
00:14:51,136 --> 00:14:53,406
Geyhatu knows about everything.

125
00:14:54,628 --> 00:14:57,238
He does not want any
troubles near the border.

126
00:14:58,150 --> 00:15:00,230
What does he want then, Alişar Bey?

127
00:15:00,230 --> 00:15:01,670
What does he want?

128
00:15:01,670 --> 00:15:04,700
To surrender rabid dogs like Balgay?

129
00:15:04,938 --> 00:15:09,658
Or to bow him and be silent
about his cruelties?

130
00:15:10,009 --> 00:15:13,409
I want to keep Geyhatu away
from the borders, Bamsı Bey.

131
00:15:14,767 --> 00:15:18,217
My duty here is taking Osman to Konya.

132
00:15:18,979 --> 00:15:23,599
Geyhatu wants to learn about the Laws of
Genghis Khan and Balgay’s outcome.

133
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:27,853
Or else, he will come here in person.

134
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:35,070
If Geyhatu comes, all the Tents will miss
Balgay’s presence around here.

135
00:15:37,773 --> 00:15:39,833
Alişar Bey…

136
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:42,490
…Osman is not here at the moment.

137
00:15:42,876 --> 00:15:45,116
Even if he was here…

138
00:15:45,116 --> 00:15:50,256
…neither your power nor Geyhatu’s
would be enough for taking him away.

139
00:15:53,076 --> 00:15:56,036
The era of tyranny has come
to an end, Alişar Bey.

140
00:15:56,142 --> 00:15:58,812
From now on, only our weapons will talk.

141
00:16:00,168 --> 00:16:03,498
He who speaks with weapons will only
get hushed by weapons.

142
00:16:04,055 --> 00:16:06,050
We fear nobody.

143
00:16:09,642 --> 00:16:12,862
However, you should know that...

144
00:16:13,181 --> 00:16:16,931
... Geyhatu is not happy with what
Balgay does these days.

145
00:16:20,623 --> 00:16:23,873
I came here to do what Geyhatu desires…

146
00:16:25,711 --> 00:16:28,344
… and to propose a deal.

147
00:16:28,344 --> 00:16:34,494
Us, Kayıs, don’t like both flourished
words and men, Alişar Bey.

148
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:39,060
Tell us whatever you want to tell already.

149
00:16:39,299 --> 00:16:41,849
Balgay will not stop as
long as he is alive.

150
00:16:42,468 --> 00:16:44,828
We all know that very well.

151
00:16:45,894 --> 00:16:48,954
Let’s fight against Balgay together.

152
00:16:49,769 --> 00:16:53,769
The hostility between Balgay
and Geyhatu will make us stronger.

153
00:16:56,844 --> 00:16:59,014
We share common interests.

154
00:17:00,413 --> 00:17:06,513
Also may you not forget that
what goes around comes around.

155
00:17:08,173 --> 00:17:09,923
Everybody leaves…

156
00:17:11,118 --> 00:17:12,928
...Alişar stays.

157
00:17:18,073 --> 00:17:22,073
Let’s say we agree with
your banner lordship…

158
00:17:24,243 --> 00:17:27,243
…what are we going to get
in return, Alişar Bey?

159
00:17:28,055 --> 00:17:30,135
Are you going to try killing me again...

160
00:17:30,135 --> 00:17:33,685
...and trouble our Tent
with all kinds of disorders?

161
00:17:35,079 --> 00:17:38,399
You would have been dead
already if I really wanted.

162
00:17:38,756 --> 00:17:41,086
And you wouldn’t be standing in front me.

163
00:17:43,036 --> 00:17:45,226
When it comes to your question, however…

164
00:17:47,938 --> 00:17:50,508
…Kayı Tent will get what it desires.

165
00:17:51,528 --> 00:17:54,508
And will be free do whatever
it wants to do with them.

166
00:17:57,001 --> 00:18:00,031
Also nothing will happen to Osman.

167
00:18:03,952 --> 00:18:06,322
What do you say, Gündüz Bey?

168
00:18:28,801 --> 00:18:30,431
Bala, my daughter.

169
00:18:31,125 --> 00:18:34,835
That impudent named Alişar is here again.

170
00:18:35,511 --> 00:18:37,521
So I heard, my daughter.

171
00:18:37,738 --> 00:18:41,738
I was about to go find out
why he came and what he wants.

172
00:18:43,406 --> 00:18:46,506
I’m afraid he came back much
stronger than he was, Selcan Hatun.

173
00:18:46,733 --> 00:18:49,863
He is gonna try to stick to
our collar even worse now.

174
00:18:50,499 --> 00:18:53,389
Just as we were about
to get rid of Mongols.

175
00:18:54,367 --> 00:18:57,377
I hope Gündüz does
not show his soft side to him.

176
00:18:57,377 --> 00:18:59,257
Also, Osman is not here.

177
00:18:59,736 --> 00:19:04,036
If we surrender to that kinless now, he
will become troublesome in the future.

178
00:19:06,464 --> 00:19:07,744
Let’s go.

179
00:19:07,953 --> 00:19:10,183
There is also something else.

180
00:19:10,753 --> 00:19:13,323
What’s that, my daughter?

181
00:19:13,323 --> 00:19:15,603
Perhaps, we can find a solution.

182
00:19:17,348 --> 00:19:19,698
That impudent named Alişar...

183
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:27,320
... once asked for my father’s
permission to get married to me.

184
00:19:30,037 --> 00:19:32,467
What are you saying, Bala?

185
00:19:34,203 --> 00:19:37,053
- Doesn't Osman know about this?
- No.

186
00:19:37,053 --> 00:19:38,313
Nobody does.

187
00:19:38,542 --> 00:19:40,412
Please keep it as a secret.

188
00:19:44,034 --> 00:19:46,174
Don’t you worry, my daughter.

189
00:19:46,174 --> 00:19:47,914
I will not tell anybody.

190
00:19:49,045 --> 00:19:51,145
It is good that you told me about this.

191
00:19:52,127 --> 00:19:54,447
If Osman learns,
he will not let him live.

192
00:19:55,363 --> 00:19:58,503
Even it means another
dirt would be removed from the world.

193
00:19:58,645 --> 00:20:02,645
However, I fear something
bad would happen to Osman.

194
00:20:04,117 --> 00:20:08,117
Let’s be patient, my daughter.

195
00:20:09,218 --> 00:20:10,508
Let's go.

196
00:20:29,711 --> 00:20:32,271
We will set the ambush
behind of Black Forest.

197
00:20:32,271 --> 00:20:33,931
Is Balgay going to use that route?

198
00:20:33,931 --> 00:20:35,351
Not Balgay…

199
00:20:35,752 --> 00:20:39,752
…but the caravan that carries
the Byzantine Princess Adelfa.

200
00:20:40,201 --> 00:20:43,131
My Bey, what business do we
have with the Byzantine Princess.

201
00:20:43,131 --> 00:20:45,881
They want to make Adelfa and
Geyhatu get married

202
00:20:45,881 --> 00:20:48,651
... so that they can
establish Byzantine-Mongol alliance.

203
00:20:50,009 --> 00:20:52,299
We will prevent that.

204
00:20:52,707 --> 00:20:54,987
My Bey, we are only two here.

205
00:20:54,987 --> 00:20:57,957
- I will go to Tent and let the Alps know.
- No, Boran.

206
00:20:58,492 --> 00:21:02,492
This mission is very important and secret.

207
00:21:04,371 --> 00:21:06,111
We will handle it together.

208
00:21:06,907 --> 00:21:08,737
As you wish, my Bey.

209
00:21:15,467 --> 00:21:17,787
Your proposal sounds courageous.

210
00:21:18,183 --> 00:21:20,083
Just like you my Bey.

211
00:21:20,906 --> 00:21:24,386
Both your weapon and
your mind are skillful.

212
00:21:25,532 --> 00:21:30,782
During hard times like this,
it is important to decide wisely.

213
00:21:38,769 --> 00:21:45,339
We managed to defend
ourselves from the tyranny of Balgay.

214
00:21:45,837 --> 00:21:49,327
But we have no problems with Geyhatu.

215
00:21:51,513 --> 00:21:57,163
Gündüz Bey, the owner of the dog
should be found as guilty as its pet.

216
00:21:57,806 --> 00:22:00,176
Geyhatu has lots of dogs.

217
00:22:03,599 --> 00:22:07,599
Bamsı Bey, how can
we deal with all of them?

218
00:22:13,497 --> 00:22:21,617
We are determined to pay taxes to Geyhatu,
and live a comfortable life, Alişar Bey.

219
00:22:21,831 --> 00:22:26,521
This decision must be made
by all of the Beys.

220
00:22:26,809 --> 00:22:30,159
We have lots of martyrs.
Our people are sick.

221
00:22:30,159 --> 00:22:34,059
You can not decide by your
own like this, Gündüz Bey.

222
00:22:34,059 --> 00:22:38,599
If you are the one who is the Bey
of Tent, go sit on that peltry.

223
00:22:38,942 --> 00:22:45,262
If you are not, try to shut up
for a while, Bamsı Bey.

224
00:22:47,035 --> 00:22:49,495
Once a Muslim is bitten by a snake...

225
00:22:49,495 --> 00:22:54,355
...he can not get bitten again
by the same snake, Gündüz Bey.

226
00:22:55,321 --> 00:22:57,471
They want to poison you.

227
00:22:58,034 --> 00:22:59,714
Don’t you understand?

228
00:23:04,403 --> 00:23:13,583
Osman has left to defend the Tent
against the anger of Geyhatu and Balgay.

229
00:23:13,712 --> 00:23:19,192
As a Bannerlord, you are the only person
who can find out where he is.

230
00:23:20,677 --> 00:23:23,837
Osman is not our problem anymore.

231
00:23:25,331 --> 00:23:31,841
Alişar Bey said ‘’If Geyhatu comes,
you will miss Balgay.’’

232
00:23:32,761 --> 00:23:35,961
Yet it’s the first day and
we already miss Dündar.

233
00:23:38,875 --> 00:23:40,385
Gündüz Bey.

234
00:23:41,234 --> 00:23:45,234
You can easily burn this Tent
with your unwise decisions.

235
00:23:47,086 --> 00:23:49,696
You're making a big mistake.

236
00:24:06,243 --> 00:24:08,743
Bamsı Bey doesn't know
much about politics.

237
00:24:10,676 --> 00:24:13,086
Your job is hard, Gündüz Bey.

238
00:24:14,963 --> 00:24:17,283
I have one more thing to say to you.

239
00:24:26,596 --> 00:24:27,836
Bamsı Bey.

240
00:24:29,350 --> 00:24:31,410
What is it Dumrul?
What's the hurry?

241
00:24:31,731 --> 00:24:33,551
My Bey, Abdurrahman Gazi...

242
00:24:34,260 --> 00:24:35,880
What about Abdurrahman Gazi?

243
00:24:36,463 --> 00:24:40,323
We found him in the woods,
he's heavily wounded, my Bey.

244
00:24:41,567 --> 00:24:42,807
Erkut Alp...

245
00:24:49,733 --> 00:24:51,713
Abdurrahman Gazi, where is he?

246
00:24:51,785 --> 00:24:56,375
My Bey, they put him in the sledge and
brought him to the medical tent.

247
00:24:56,524 --> 00:25:00,894
- No, not the medical tent, Dumrul!
- My Bey, he's heavily wounded!

248
00:25:00,951 --> 00:25:06,331
It's my Osman's command, don't you know?
There are Bey's that's loyal to Dündar...

249
00:25:06,331 --> 00:25:08,111
... we can't know what they'll do!

250
00:25:10,228 --> 00:25:11,448
Dumrul...

251
00:25:12,329 --> 00:25:17,179
... until I say otherwise, everyone will
know Abdurrahman Gazi as dead.

252
00:25:17,179 --> 00:25:23,939
We will treat him outside the Tent. Run to
the medical tent and get what's needed.

253
00:25:24,368 --> 00:25:28,818
Then inform Gündüz Bey,
without that Alişar dog hearing it.

254
00:25:28,907 --> 00:25:32,907
- Thank you.
- Come on, boy! Come on!

255
00:25:33,751 --> 00:25:35,831
Come on boy.

256
00:25:59,473 --> 00:26:01,593
Princess can't get to Konya.

257
00:26:02,013 --> 00:26:05,373
No one from her convoy will survive.

258
00:26:05,722 --> 00:26:07,472
Are we going to kill Princess too?

259
00:26:07,957 --> 00:26:10,357
It's not like us to kill
an innocent woman.

260
00:26:10,910 --> 00:26:13,230
If we can capture her alive, good.

261
00:26:14,078 --> 00:26:15,078
But...

262
00:26:16,605 --> 00:26:21,025
... if our mission is endangered,
you know what to do.

263
00:26:21,025 --> 00:26:27,105
I know, my Bey. When the fire starts,
Allah doesn't pick trees.

264
00:26:34,971 --> 00:26:36,451
Here they come, Boran.

265
00:26:46,369 --> 00:26:48,059
My Bey, they're too little.

266
00:26:52,425 --> 00:26:56,765
They trust themselves too much
when they are in their own land.

267
00:26:56,835 --> 00:26:59,375
That's why they will get caught off guard.

268
00:27:52,922 --> 00:27:54,372
Abdurrahman...

269
00:27:57,262 --> 00:28:01,492
Abdurrahman, who did
this to you, brother?

270
00:28:01,713 --> 00:28:03,683
Who did this to you, brother?

271
00:28:05,581 --> 00:28:07,461
Open your eyes.

272
00:28:08,647 --> 00:28:13,927
What will I say to my Ertuğrul Bey
if something happens to you, huh?

273
00:28:14,687 --> 00:28:20,827
What will I say to my Ertuğrul Bey?
Open your eyes, brother, be strong!

274
00:28:31,721 --> 00:28:35,011
He has a pulse, he's breathing,
he'll be okay, right Ayaz?

275
00:28:35,223 --> 00:28:37,443
He has a pulse but it's slow, my Bey.

276
00:28:38,794 --> 00:28:40,944
He had lost too much
blood when I found him.

277
00:28:41,248 --> 00:28:44,318
You cauterized the wound,
the bleeding stopped!

278
00:28:45,250 --> 00:28:51,100
Then why don't you open your eyes?
Open your eyes, brother!

279
00:28:57,920 --> 00:29:00,610
Kılıç! How is Kılıç Alp?

280
00:29:00,984 --> 00:29:04,264
Both Kılıç Alp and Abdurrahman
Gazi are strong, my Bey.

281
00:29:04,330 --> 00:29:05,330
He is.

282
00:29:07,136 --> 00:29:15,186
He is strong, he is Abdurrahman Gazi! He
is like a lion! My brother is like a lion!

283
00:29:19,117 --> 00:29:22,087
But Erkut didn't make it, my Bey.

284
00:29:25,611 --> 00:29:26,691
I know.

285
00:29:28,090 --> 00:29:29,260
I know.

286
00:29:42,622 --> 00:29:46,962
My Allah, My Great Allah...

287
00:29:47,669 --> 00:29:53,229
The intention of the valiants who
pass away is your gratitude.

288
00:29:54,087 --> 00:29:58,087
My Allah, may you...

289
00:29:58,590 --> 00:30:01,250
... may you accept them in your place.

290
00:30:01,889 --> 00:30:03,869
Accept them in your place.

291
00:30:29,083 --> 00:30:33,083
They attacked them to get Dündar out.

292
00:30:33,583 --> 00:30:35,343
Who could've done this, my Bey?

293
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:39,120
Ayaz, Ayaz...

294
00:30:39,565 --> 00:30:43,565
Dündar is gone, Alişar is in the Tent.

295
00:30:47,421 --> 00:30:50,341
Something is fishy here, Ayaz.

296
00:30:55,780 --> 00:31:03,260
Everybody will know Abdurrahman
Gazi as dead until Osman comes.

297
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:07,560
- We will treat him here.
- As you say, my Bey.

298
00:31:10,397 --> 00:31:13,477
Oh, my brother! Oh, my brother!

299
00:31:13,738 --> 00:31:16,728
Come on, open your eyes.

300
00:31:19,227 --> 00:31:21,837
Oh, great Abdurrahman Gazi.

301
00:31:23,517 --> 00:31:25,887
Open your eyes, my valiant brother.

302
00:31:45,300 --> 00:31:46,510
Now.

303
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:50,880
Allahu Akbar!

304
00:31:52,055 --> 00:31:53,725
Allahu Akbar!

305
00:31:54,939 --> 00:31:56,819
Allahu Akbar!

306
00:32:01,047 --> 00:32:02,977
Allahu Akbar!

307
00:32:11,471 --> 00:32:12,931
Allahu Akbar!

308
00:32:17,322 --> 00:32:18,822
Allahu Akbar!

309
00:33:30,019 --> 00:33:31,269
Princess.

310
00:33:32,789 --> 00:33:34,169
Come outside.

311
00:33:49,232 --> 00:33:52,062
You won't kill me, will you?

312
00:34:02,187 --> 00:34:06,567
We've come here for life, not death.

313
00:34:11,377 --> 00:34:14,477
And there's nobody here that can hurt you.

314
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:24,880
But I'm... I'm not the Princess.

315
00:34:27,652 --> 00:34:29,312
What do you mean?

316
00:34:34,564 --> 00:34:37,244
- Who are you?
- I'm...

317
00:35:00,420 --> 00:35:03,860
It seems both you and the
Princess are in danger.

318
00:35:04,747 --> 00:35:07,407
I will do whatever I can to save you.

319
00:35:08,823 --> 00:35:12,253
Tell me, tell me who you are.

320
00:35:12,651 --> 00:35:14,141
Who are you?

321
00:35:24,214 --> 00:35:25,904
She's still alive, my Bey.

322
00:35:45,224 --> 00:35:47,544
My condolences, Zöhre Hatun.

323
00:35:48,625 --> 00:35:51,155
Thank you, Alişar Bey.

324
00:35:51,589 --> 00:35:54,269
They took down my mountain, Dündar.

325
00:35:54,614 --> 00:35:57,614
An ember burns where it falls, I know.

326
00:35:58,112 --> 00:36:02,372
But what you need is
not anger, but strength.

327
00:36:20,200 --> 00:36:22,810
We've discussed with Gündüz Bey.

328
00:36:24,094 --> 00:36:27,014
I want to take you to my
mansion, if you want.

329
00:36:27,539 --> 00:36:31,539
You will be comfortable in
the banner lord's mansion.

330
00:36:32,141 --> 00:36:39,591
When our wounds heal, we will arrange
our cancelled marriage in a modest way.

331
00:36:41,389 --> 00:36:43,419
You have my consent.

332
00:36:48,799 --> 00:36:50,489
I want to get out of...

333
00:36:52,402 --> 00:36:56,402
... this Tent that's
turned into a warzone.

334
00:36:56,402 --> 00:37:00,072
Your anger and grudge is the
reason this Tent is restless.

335
00:37:00,168 --> 00:37:02,288
Two lives were taken because of you.

336
00:37:02,624 --> 00:37:04,664
Are you still not satisfied?

337
00:37:07,193 --> 00:37:08,383
Selcan Hatun.

338
00:37:09,599 --> 00:37:14,019
We know you, we know you very well.

339
00:37:15,051 --> 00:37:19,541
Your life is full of squabble and words.

340
00:37:20,326 --> 00:37:25,676
I understand that, but our wound is fresh!

341
00:37:26,078 --> 00:37:28,668
Would you shut up? Shut up.

342
00:37:29,447 --> 00:37:35,837
Stay away, Selcan Hatun!
The fire within me rises to my head!

343
00:37:36,017 --> 00:37:38,397
Don't let my anger burn you!

344
00:37:44,431 --> 00:37:47,711
I don't want to stay in the Tent
and get myself in trouble.

345
00:37:48,401 --> 00:37:53,281
Since you are so kind,
you have my consent too.

346
00:37:53,625 --> 00:37:57,625
We'll prepare and come to your mansion.

347
00:38:00,660 --> 00:38:01,890
But...

348
00:38:03,682 --> 00:38:05,592
... I won't leave my son here.

349
00:38:11,289 --> 00:38:12,709
Gündüz Bey...

350
00:38:14,163 --> 00:38:20,393
... allow me to bury him someplace
I want with my own hands.

351
00:38:24,148 --> 00:38:28,528
Batur's death was not enough, now you
are trying to take him away from his home?

352
00:38:29,512 --> 00:38:30,792
Aunt.

353
00:38:31,907 --> 00:38:36,487
What a pity that you don't even
deserve your son's corpse.

354
00:38:37,180 --> 00:38:40,630
You and Dündar are the
ones who brought this to us!

355
00:38:41,168 --> 00:38:46,068
You killed your son! Now let him
sleep with his ancestors in his grave.

356
00:38:46,193 --> 00:38:47,493
Aunt, I said!

357
00:38:47,814 --> 00:38:52,824
Even if you are his mother,
Batur is Süleyman Şah's grandson!

358
00:38:55,012 --> 00:38:57,202
His place is here.

359
00:38:58,631 --> 00:39:01,101
No one will give you his corpse!

360
00:39:01,101 --> 00:39:02,011
Enough!

361
00:39:04,970 --> 00:39:09,390
Since when people say
something after Bey's words?

362
00:39:10,108 --> 00:39:12,028
Don't you hear what she says?

363
00:39:12,712 --> 00:39:14,712
They did all these games,

364
00:39:15,175 --> 00:39:19,785
They allied with the Mongols and
attacked Osman in the Tent!

365
00:39:22,179 --> 00:39:24,279
Selcan Hatun is right, Gündüz Bey!

366
00:39:25,275 --> 00:39:29,445
We like guests when they
know their place, Bala Hatun.

367
00:39:30,681 --> 00:39:32,551
Don't go too far!

368
00:39:36,795 --> 00:39:41,515
Bala is my girl,
she's not a guest in the Tent.

369
00:39:41,997 --> 00:39:44,677
And the things she said aren't lies!

370
00:39:45,252 --> 00:39:48,332
When did you forget all these?

371
00:39:48,994 --> 00:39:51,214
If Bala is your girl...

372
00:39:51,776 --> 00:39:56,356
... then take your girl
and go to your tent.

373
00:39:57,161 --> 00:39:58,191
Go!

374
00:40:01,190 --> 00:40:04,000
Don't make me do
something I'll regret, aunt!

375
00:40:23,617 --> 00:40:24,447
Alps!

376
00:40:26,249 --> 00:40:27,689
Arrange a cart.

377
00:40:29,180 --> 00:40:34,330
You will deliver Batur's
funeral to Zöhre Hatun.

378
00:40:45,310 --> 00:40:47,810
If you are not Princess Adelfa...

379
00:40:47,810 --> 00:40:49,560
... then where is she?

380
00:40:50,471 --> 00:40:53,471
I can't tell you that!

381
00:40:54,032 --> 00:40:59,272
We both know that Princess wouldn't
be a wife to a Mongolian bear willingly.

382
00:40:59,864 --> 00:41:05,164
It doesn't matter! If not him,
someone else will take her!

383
00:41:06,967 --> 00:41:11,747
We are Turk. We would
never hurt an innocent woman.

384
00:41:13,429 --> 00:41:17,429
Remember how I treated you when
I thought you were the Princess.

385
00:41:19,884 --> 00:41:24,624
I fear that she will get hurt!

386
00:41:25,305 --> 00:41:29,605
If you don't tell me where
Princess is, then she will get hurt.

387
00:41:29,889 --> 00:41:31,459
Because of you.

388
00:41:35,837 --> 00:41:38,047
They will take Princess Adelfa...

389
00:41:42,448 --> 00:41:44,778
... to Engürü road.

390
00:41:49,715 --> 00:41:53,715
Please, treat her well.

391
00:42:06,306 --> 00:42:08,396
Byzantine's games never end.

392
00:42:09,187 --> 00:42:12,627
Neither our thirst for death!

393
00:42:12,721 --> 00:42:14,071
Yes, my Bey!

394
00:42:14,724 --> 00:42:17,554
This convoy was a trap
for precaution then.

395
00:42:18,388 --> 00:42:20,078
But why did they do it?

396
00:42:20,078 --> 00:42:22,748
We'll find out when they face us, Boran.

397
00:42:24,437 --> 00:42:27,457
We will pass through the mountains
and go to the Engürü road.

398
00:42:35,853 --> 00:42:37,823
This is the path they'll take.

399
00:42:39,279 --> 00:42:44,269
We will make our ambush right there.

400
00:42:46,541 --> 00:42:51,401
If one person survives,
Geyhatu will know it's us.

401
00:42:51,707 --> 00:42:54,887
- And Princess?
- She will die too.

402
00:42:58,923 --> 00:43:00,453
What is it Cerkutay?

403
00:43:01,330 --> 00:43:03,590
You are sweating like an ox with a plow!

404
00:43:03,662 --> 00:43:07,852
Osman is hunting Geyhatu's
soldiers that guard the cart.

405
00:43:12,198 --> 00:43:15,478
Then there's no need for us to attack.

406
00:43:15,790 --> 00:43:18,720
We will let Osman serve us.

407
00:43:20,591 --> 00:43:25,451
Let him clean the scales,
then we will take the fish.

408
00:43:26,815 --> 00:43:30,945
What does Osman want with the Princess?

409
00:43:31,888 --> 00:43:36,698
It seems that the ones who gave
Osman Genghis Khan's Laws...

410
00:43:37,532 --> 00:43:40,962
... now want the Princess.

411
00:43:41,095 --> 00:43:44,205
Who does Osman work with,
Commander Balgay?

412
00:43:46,471 --> 00:43:49,911
With the dark spirits,
don't you see?

413
00:43:50,291 --> 00:43:54,811
We will let Osman do our job.

414
00:43:54,811 --> 00:43:55,581
Then...

415
00:43:56,651 --> 00:44:00,981
... we will take care of him.

416
00:44:07,272 --> 00:44:13,892
Be ready, the spirits that left me
starting to get closer to me.

417
00:44:14,912 --> 00:44:20,602
I feel it in my veins that
carry ember for blood!

418
00:44:21,382 --> 00:44:25,382
Erlik Han, may happiness be yours...

419
00:44:26,407 --> 00:44:28,017
... and blood be mine.

420
00:44:52,084 --> 00:44:54,294
Are you ready, Commander Salvador?

421
00:44:54,294 --> 00:44:56,334
We will go with 20 soldiers, Princess.

422
00:44:56,702 --> 00:45:01,482
I will look for Osman's traces by
going to every secret place of his I know.

423
00:45:02,436 --> 00:45:06,436
Maybe you'll find Osman himself
while you were looking for his traces.

424
00:45:09,780 --> 00:45:12,660
If with God's help, I find
him, I will be honored...

425
00:45:12,660 --> 00:45:15,900
to throw his corpse
to your feet, Princess.

426
00:45:30,718 --> 00:45:35,568
How well he plays, while
looking at our eyes, traitor!

427
00:45:37,245 --> 00:45:39,445
And we are watching him, Helen?

428
00:45:42,006 --> 00:45:43,056
Is it bad?

429
00:45:48,539 --> 00:45:51,989
Dündar Bey will take the Tent back.

430
00:45:54,185 --> 00:45:56,905
Alişar is the banner lord like before.

431
00:45:56,932 --> 00:46:00,392
So, Alişar will herd Dündar and
the other sheeps near him.

432
00:46:01,602 --> 00:46:05,102
Since we have the Genghis Laws with us...

433
00:46:06,459 --> 00:46:08,839
... we will herd Alişar.

434
00:46:11,983 --> 00:46:13,733
Don't worry, Helen.

435
00:46:15,762 --> 00:46:18,032
Fortune favors us.

436
00:46:19,870 --> 00:46:24,290
We are slowly getting closer
to get rid of Osman!

437
00:46:27,539 --> 00:46:28,879
Princess...

438
00:46:30,618 --> 00:46:32,528
I haven't seen Master Yannis?

439
00:46:33,001 --> 00:46:35,141
He went to the Margaret Monastery.

440
00:46:37,952 --> 00:46:41,012
He gave you a mission.

441
00:46:42,065 --> 00:46:45,215
A Byzantine Princess is on
the road from Nicaea.

442
00:46:45,215 --> 00:46:50,735
Master Yannis was worried about her.
He wants you to...

443
00:46:51,178 --> 00:46:53,798
... go after her with a special team.

444
00:46:56,509 --> 00:46:57,499
Now...

445
00:46:59,396 --> 00:46:59,552
... listen to my words carefully.

446
00:46:59,552 --> 00:47:01,616
Listen carefully to what I'm gonna say.
... listen to my words carefully.

447
00:47:01,616 --> 00:47:01,802
Listen carefully to what I'm gonna say.

448
00:47:13,728 --> 00:47:15,488
My brave fellow.

449
00:47:16,965 --> 00:47:18,985
My confidant.

450
00:47:20,863 --> 00:47:22,153
My brother.

451
00:47:22,805 --> 00:47:24,585
Abdurrahman Gazi.

452
00:47:25,542 --> 00:47:28,082
The uncontrolled lion of the Kayı.

453
00:47:28,569 --> 00:47:30,619
Stay strong, Abdurrahman Gazi.

454
00:47:30,791 --> 00:47:32,521
Stay strong my brave man.

455
00:48:01,564 --> 00:48:03,434
What's the news, Bamsi Bey?

456
00:48:12,890 --> 00:48:15,130
Abdurrahman Gazi is my father's entrusted.

457
00:48:19,165 --> 00:48:23,525
Kılıç is not just my helper.

458
00:48:24,478 --> 00:48:27,558
He is my fellow, he is my confidant.

459
00:48:30,503 --> 00:48:32,983
I know, Gunduz.

460
00:48:35,582 --> 00:48:36,542
Gunduz.

461
00:48:37,329 --> 00:48:40,379
Did Alisar become suspicious about it?

462
00:48:41,464 --> 00:48:42,934
I don't think so.

463
00:48:43,181 --> 00:48:44,701
Well done, son.

464
00:48:45,117 --> 00:48:47,417
You've deceived this half breed
Mongol dog.

465
00:48:49,420 --> 00:48:51,610
What Osman said came out right.

466
00:48:51,941 --> 00:48:56,121
With the corpse of Dundar Bey, we see
those who got our father into trouble.

467
00:48:57,961 --> 00:49:00,191
We learned to fight with perfidious...

468
00:49:00,278 --> 00:49:02,138
...and clash with unbeliever...

469
00:49:02,270 --> 00:49:03,770
...in your tent, Bamsi Bey.

470
00:49:06,633 --> 00:49:09,473
I'm not regretful for all efforts
I spent on you, son.

471
00:49:09,803 --> 00:49:10,913
I'm not.

472
00:49:11,059 --> 00:49:12,809
You've gained my admiration.

473
00:49:14,601 --> 00:49:15,731
From now on.

474
00:49:16,072 --> 00:49:19,042
From now on, the end of the road
has appeared, son.

475
00:49:20,454 --> 00:49:22,494
Alisar's life journey came to an end.

476
00:49:22,959 --> 00:49:27,139
But, there will be a lot of foxes
around you.

477
00:49:27,579 --> 00:49:31,129
In this hard time, as you want to take
Aygul and Zohre...

478
00:49:32,094 --> 00:49:34,474
...Dundar Bey should be with Alisar.

479
00:49:34,857 --> 00:49:35,617
My son.

480
00:49:35,930 --> 00:49:39,360
We don't need suspicion but proof.

481
00:49:40,176 --> 00:49:42,496
That's easy with the help of
Allah, Bamsi Bey.

482
00:49:43,420 --> 00:49:46,440
I will send the soldiers to escort the
car carrying them.

483
00:49:48,138 --> 00:49:50,178
We need to find Dundar Bey.

484
00:49:50,632 --> 00:49:52,452
Long live with your wisdom, son.

485
00:49:52,515 --> 00:49:54,385
Long live with your wisdom.

486
00:49:54,674 --> 00:49:57,214
When the news we're waiting for
appear...

487
00:49:57,333 --> 00:49:59,503
...and we find the trace of Dundar Bey...

488
00:49:59,578 --> 00:50:02,308
...then it means Alisar will die.

489
00:50:07,220 --> 00:50:13,350
My Gunduz.
We owe you running over the Alisar...

490
00:50:13,494 --> 00:50:15,904
...under the stones of his mansion, son.

491
00:51:24,789 --> 00:51:26,949
Maybe, it is our destiny.

492
00:51:28,391 --> 00:51:31,681
We are deprived of both our tent...

493
00:51:32,509 --> 00:51:35,219
...and our life.

494
00:51:40,503 --> 00:51:44,103
We are worse than those who
we thought they were miserable.

495
00:51:49,918 --> 00:51:51,928
May Allah give us power.

496
00:51:52,965 --> 00:51:54,095
My Allah.

497
00:51:55,981 --> 00:51:59,601
May Allah give us power...

498
00:51:59,795 --> 00:52:01,395
...to bear this pain.

499
00:52:25,505 --> 00:52:29,825
I wish I could say welcome cheerfully.

500
00:52:30,202 --> 00:52:33,082
But, It didn't happen.

501
00:52:35,815 --> 00:52:37,755
Those who come together in pain...

502
00:52:38,672 --> 00:52:40,592
...connect each other stronger.

503
00:52:45,013 --> 00:52:48,293
My home is your home.

504
00:52:49,801 --> 00:52:52,511
It may not destroy your pain at all...

505
00:52:52,830 --> 00:52:56,070
...but it'll relieve you.

506
00:53:15,401 --> 00:53:16,621
Dundar Bey.

507
00:53:17,631 --> 00:53:18,821
Father.

508
00:53:31,993 --> 00:53:33,613
Father!

509
00:53:36,805 --> 00:53:38,895
Father.

510
00:53:42,353 --> 00:53:43,313
Father.

511
00:53:43,545 --> 00:53:44,275
Father.

512
00:53:46,946 --> 00:53:48,086
Father.

513
00:53:48,157 --> 00:53:49,077
Father.

514
00:53:51,013 --> 00:53:52,113
Father.

515
00:53:52,238 --> 00:53:53,108
Father.

516
00:53:55,485 --> 00:53:56,505
Father.

517
00:53:56,773 --> 00:53:57,783
Father.

518
00:53:58,601 --> 00:53:59,691
Father, We...

519
00:53:59,951 --> 00:54:01,781
They couldn't, my daughter.

520
00:54:02,614 --> 00:54:04,154
They couldn't.

521
00:54:04,554 --> 00:54:06,644
Don't be afraid.

522
00:54:08,105 --> 00:54:10,015
I'm here, my Aygul.

523
00:54:10,273 --> 00:54:11,653
Your father is here.

524
00:54:11,864 --> 00:54:14,364
Don't scare, my daughter.
Don't.

525
00:54:19,224 --> 00:54:20,494
Alisar Bey....

526
00:54:21,330 --> 00:54:23,410
...saved me from them.

527
00:54:26,667 --> 00:54:27,967
They couldn't.

528
00:54:33,905 --> 00:54:34,905
My husband..

529
00:54:35,055 --> 00:54:37,005
Fortunately, you're alive.

530
00:54:37,497 --> 00:54:39,477
You're here, my husband.

531
00:55:31,956 --> 00:55:33,086
Batur.

532
00:55:49,723 --> 00:55:51,353
My brave son.

533
00:55:53,568 --> 00:55:55,388
My precious.

534
00:55:58,113 --> 00:55:59,353
My son.

535
00:56:00,180 --> 00:56:01,200
My son.

536
00:56:09,635 --> 00:56:13,195
You're too young to die.

537
00:56:15,392 --> 00:56:19,582
You're too young to fade away, my son.

538
00:56:26,292 --> 00:56:27,572
Dundar Bey.

539
00:56:35,376 --> 00:56:40,256
I will call those who did it to
you to account, my son.

540
00:56:41,691 --> 00:56:45,181
I promise I will.

541
00:56:45,771 --> 00:56:47,931
Don't worry about that, my son.

542
00:56:48,466 --> 00:56:49,766
Don't.

543
00:56:50,621 --> 00:56:53,841
I will take revenge from those
who killed you.

544
00:56:54,452 --> 00:56:55,952
I will.

545
00:57:01,997 --> 00:57:06,197
Thanks to me, Osman became the
enemy of your father.

546
00:57:06,841 --> 00:57:09,851
Thanks to you. Dundar will be
the enemy of Osman.

547
00:57:10,123 --> 00:57:12,763
They will shed each other's blood.

548
00:57:13,388 --> 00:57:19,198
Then, Geyhatu will punish Balgay.

549
00:57:20,647 --> 00:57:24,917
I will make all of my enemy fight
against each other.

550
00:57:32,768 --> 00:57:34,788
We will take revenge surely.

551
00:57:35,528 --> 00:57:39,288
We will surely catch those who
got us into this condition...

552
00:57:39,463 --> 00:57:41,743
...and made us have this pain.

553
00:57:46,284 --> 00:57:48,544
I could say how we will do this.

554
00:57:49,327 --> 00:57:51,047
But Allah is great.

555
00:57:51,716 --> 00:57:53,976
Now it's their turn to die.

556
00:57:54,622 --> 00:57:56,312
Their turn, my daughter.

557
00:57:57,840 --> 00:57:59,210
Their turn.

558
00:58:00,817 --> 00:58:03,867
We'll stand against them rigidly,
Dundar Bey.

559
00:58:04,259 --> 00:58:08,469
Now we have both the power
and the control.

560
00:58:10,120 --> 00:58:14,460
We should bury him immediately.

561
00:58:17,508 --> 00:58:21,238
I will bury my pain with my son.

562
00:58:21,402 --> 00:58:26,212
But my anger is my dog.

563
00:58:26,353 --> 00:58:30,563
My anger always will come with me.

564
00:58:32,597 --> 00:58:39,497
From now on, they will see another
Dundar against them.

565
00:58:39,755 --> 00:58:42,765
I will crush them like an insect.

566
00:58:42,991 --> 00:58:44,661
I will crush them.

567
00:58:47,605 --> 00:58:49,485
I will crush them like an insect.

568
00:58:52,108 --> 00:58:53,108
My son.

569
00:58:54,192 --> 00:58:55,552
My brave man.

570
00:58:57,135 --> 00:59:02,365
I promise I will crush all of
them like an insect.

571
01:00:01,106 --> 01:00:02,396
Come this way.

572
01:00:04,185 --> 01:00:05,785
Hurry! Let's go!

573
01:00:11,900 --> 01:00:13,920
Don't stray from the troop.

574
01:00:14,119 --> 01:00:15,309
I'm coming as well.

575
01:00:58,986 --> 01:01:01,086
I need to deliver it to Bamsi Bey.

576
01:02:51,017 --> 01:02:52,637
Wake up.

577
01:02:54,628 --> 01:02:56,008
The rest is blessing.

578
01:02:56,124 --> 01:02:56,974
Come on.

579
01:03:08,461 --> 01:03:10,131
Look, Dundar bey.

580
01:03:12,571 --> 01:03:13,971
Your son...

581
01:03:21,673 --> 01:03:30,273
...who took all world against him for
the sake of the father of brave Batur...

582
01:03:33,031 --> 01:03:36,551
We buried our son to here, Dundar Bey.

583
01:03:41,088 --> 01:03:42,058
Ah! Ah!

584
01:03:52,065 --> 01:03:58,825
Ah! Ah!

585
01:04:00,079 --> 01:04:03,769
You've been buried into a dark soil...

586
01:04:05,535 --> 01:04:10,035
...without living your life to the
fullest, my son.

587
01:04:12,091 --> 01:04:13,161
My son.

588
01:04:17,537 --> 01:04:23,117
I wish those who killed you didn't stay
at peace in this world, my son.

589
01:04:27,041 --> 01:04:29,111
My son!

590
01:04:34,896 --> 01:04:35,956
You...

591
01:04:38,125 --> 01:04:41,575
You the son of Suleyman Sah,
Dundar Bey.

592
01:04:44,724 --> 01:04:45,624
Look around.

593
01:04:46,966 --> 01:04:52,286
Look who is with you in your son funeral.

594
01:04:53,694 --> 01:04:55,424
How many people are there?

595
01:04:59,052 --> 01:05:02,402
The one who is buried is not only my son.

596
01:05:07,653 --> 01:05:12,653
Osman buried your dignity into
this soil.

597
01:05:24,479 --> 01:05:31,789
I promise on the corpse of my son...

598
01:05:44,025 --> 01:05:50,315
...I will pull off the hands of Osman.

599
01:05:51,510 --> 01:05:53,920
The kids who see what I will do him...

600
01:05:54,082 --> 01:05:56,372
...will grow older with fear.

601
01:05:58,254 --> 01:06:02,074
I will make a road from the heads of
people who support Osman...

602
01:06:02,095 --> 01:06:04,725
...and I will walk over this road.

603
01:06:05,360 --> 01:06:08,690
I will pile up the body of headless
people...

604
01:06:08,771 --> 01:06:13,701
...and I will make a mountain from it
so that it will be a warning...

605
01:06:14,633 --> 01:06:16,543
...for those who want to be forgiven.

606
01:06:17,275 --> 01:06:18,485
A warning.

607
01:06:19,401 --> 01:06:20,821
Come on, wife.

608
01:06:22,305 --> 01:06:23,375
Come on.

609
01:07:07,058 --> 01:07:09,328
We hit the jackpot this time, my bey.

610
01:07:09,699 --> 01:07:11,959
I was so sorry for that girl.

611
01:07:12,057 --> 01:07:13,547
I hope we'll save her.

612
01:07:14,561 --> 01:07:15,771
I hope so, brother.

613
01:07:16,678 --> 01:07:17,528
I hope so.

614
01:07:31,311 --> 01:07:34,681
There isn't any place where Mongols
didn't torture.

615
01:07:34,716 --> 01:07:35,956
We saw it again.

616
01:07:39,420 --> 01:07:40,900
After you, princess.

617
01:07:48,133 --> 01:07:49,993
We'll do it silently.

618
01:07:51,360 --> 01:07:53,060
We will take the princess...

619
01:07:53,911 --> 01:07:56,071
...after Byzantium soldiers disappear..

620
01:07:57,042 --> 01:07:59,992
Be careful, Boran.

621
01:08:00,677 --> 01:08:02,747
We don't know what we'll
encounter.

622
01:08:02,915 --> 01:08:04,295
Don't worry, my bey.

623
01:08:26,816 --> 01:08:28,536
-Dundar Bey.
-Dundar Bey.

624
01:08:30,596 --> 01:08:31,516
Fortunately.

625
01:08:32,909 --> 01:08:33,989
Fortunately.

626
01:08:46,975 --> 01:08:51,785
If we're alive, its thanks to Alisar.

627
01:08:53,245 --> 01:08:56,845
He saved us from Osman.

628
01:08:57,319 --> 01:08:58,319
Thanks.

629
01:08:58,530 --> 01:08:59,600
Thanks, my bey.

630
01:09:00,183 --> 01:09:02,393
Our friendship lasts forever.

631
01:09:04,293 --> 01:09:11,473
But I am sorry that there are just
3 beys who are wise in the Kayı tents...

632
01:09:12,216 --> 01:09:13,696
I'm sorry for that.

633
01:09:17,100 --> 01:09:20,710
Now, you know me as dead.

634
01:09:21,395 --> 01:09:24,105
The power is with Osman.

635
01:09:25,002 --> 01:09:28,002
But with the help of Alisar....

636
01:09:28,614 --> 01:09:32,914
...the bloody trap that they set up
will damage all of them.

637
01:09:35,709 --> 01:09:36,939
You learned....

638
01:09:37,551 --> 01:09:41,891
...and all living creatures who are
breathing will learn.

639
01:09:43,033 --> 01:09:45,203
Whoever Alisar supports...

640
01:09:45,800 --> 01:09:47,340
...the power is with him.

641
01:09:52,022 --> 01:09:53,022
Osman.

642
01:09:53,798 --> 01:09:56,288
He made Gündüz Bey sit on the throne.

643
01:09:59,544 --> 01:10:00,445
We had to do it.

644
01:10:00,445 --> 01:10:00,817
We kissed his hand.
We had to do it.

645
01:10:00,817 --> 01:10:02,515
We kissed his hand.

646
01:10:02,952 --> 01:10:05,992
He is no different than Osman.

647
01:10:07,945 --> 01:10:09,935
What will we do now, my Bey?

648
01:10:10,525 --> 01:10:15,935
Osman killed my son Batur and spilled
the blood of a brother.

649
01:10:17,230 --> 01:10:19,970
There is no peace for us...

650
01:10:19,998 --> 01:10:21,848
...before killing Osman...

651
01:10:22,535 --> 01:10:25,465
...and those who stand before him.

652
01:10:30,630 --> 01:10:33,300
But, my Bey...

653
01:10:33,647 --> 01:10:35,987
We are low on force limits.

654
01:10:37,486 --> 01:10:40,596
You either trust in your Bey...

655
01:10:40,723 --> 01:10:44,273
...or you will stand beside Osman.

656
01:10:48,573 --> 01:10:51,553
And if you trust in your Bey...

657
01:10:51,972 --> 01:10:54,992
...you should listen to my
words carefully.

658
01:11:18,172 --> 01:11:21,412
So, you are the new woman of Geyhatu.

659
01:11:24,192 --> 01:11:26,702
We are returning to the Tent.
Hurry up, slackers.

660
01:11:29,307 --> 01:11:30,577
We are under attack.

661
01:11:36,852 --> 01:11:38,652
The princess is running away.

662
01:11:41,240 --> 01:11:44,860
Orhan, go, I'll cover you.

663
01:11:44,993 --> 01:11:45,853
Thank you, my Bey.

664
01:12:44,059 --> 01:12:45,719
Come, Gündüz.

665
01:12:54,854 --> 01:12:58,154
We'll do whatever necessary for them
to live, Bamsı Bey.

666
01:12:59,375 --> 01:13:02,805
Not being able to take him to the Tent is
heavy, son.

667
01:13:03,117 --> 01:13:07,117
Don't, Bamsı Bey. If we take him
to the oba...

668
01:13:07,246 --> 01:13:10,516
...Alişar and Dündar Bey will find out
that we know everything.

669
01:13:10,573 --> 01:13:13,503
I know, son. I know.

670
01:13:13,700 --> 01:13:15,880
Any news from Alps?

671
01:13:17,361 --> 01:13:19,751
We were right to doubt.

672
01:13:20,626 --> 01:13:24,226
So, Dündar Bey fell to Alişar's trap?

673
01:13:24,376 --> 01:13:27,676
My uncle thinks that Osman is the killer
of Batur.

674
01:13:28,276 --> 01:13:32,276
And Alişar wants to use Dündar Bey's
grief of losing a child.

675
01:13:32,349 --> 01:13:36,819
It was obvious from Alişar's venomous
snake-like behaviours.

676
01:13:37,099 --> 01:13:42,059
He sends Dündar after us, so he can wash
his dirty works with the blood spilled.

677
01:13:45,857 --> 01:13:49,857
But, son, if he planned such a ruse...

678
01:13:50,015 --> 01:13:53,325
...he'll need support from the Tent.

679
01:13:53,497 --> 01:13:58,837
And the wells that will provide to
Alişar's tent is obvious.

680
01:14:03,087 --> 01:14:04,597
Ayaz.

681
01:14:05,750 --> 01:14:07,130
Yes, my Bey.

682
01:14:07,220 --> 01:14:09,910
You'll watch Demirci Bey and Şahsin Bey
closely.

683
01:14:10,001 --> 01:14:14,001
You'll follow their every step and
every person they speak to.

684
01:14:14,796 --> 01:14:17,406
If you get suspicious of anything
send word to me.

685
01:14:17,564 --> 01:14:18,794
Yes, my Bey.

686
01:14:21,779 --> 01:14:22,939
Son,

687
01:14:23,094 --> 01:14:27,614
I'm grieved but only for the situation
of Dündar Bey.

688
01:14:28,326 --> 01:14:32,686
Now, when you learn the truth,
how will he look into our faces?

689
01:14:32,723 --> 01:14:35,693
We have to save Dündar Bey from the
hands of this snake, Bamsı Bey.

690
01:14:35,748 --> 01:14:37,628
And to do this...

691
01:14:37,696 --> 01:14:40,846
...we have to crush the nest of the snake.

692
01:14:48,980 --> 01:14:51,670
I'm sorrowful, Dündar Bey.

693
01:14:51,774 --> 01:14:54,064
We lost our child...

694
01:14:54,100 --> 01:14:57,010
We lost our home...
We lost our Tent...

695
01:14:57,252 --> 01:15:00,292
What else can Osman do to us?

696
01:15:01,882 --> 01:15:03,742
Ahh, Osman.

697
01:15:07,028 --> 01:15:08,918
Ahh, Osman.

698
01:15:12,228 --> 01:15:15,218
One who calls his madness, bravery.
One who acts on his will...

699
01:15:15,349 --> 01:15:18,359
...and call it law.

700
01:15:21,812 --> 01:15:25,372
They think the fields are theirs now.

701
01:15:26,855 --> 01:15:30,855
Let them think.
Let them enjoy it.

702
01:15:31,373 --> 01:15:36,463
Then, I'll be onto them with
all my fury.

703
01:15:36,761 --> 01:15:41,531
And I'll make his followers regret
what they did.

704
01:15:43,518 --> 01:15:45,908
We lost everything.

705
01:15:47,949 --> 01:15:51,979
How will we breathe easy?
How will these things happen?

706
01:15:51,979 --> 01:15:54,089
What are you planning, my Bey?

707
01:15:55,386 --> 01:15:58,446
Time of that will come, too, Hatun.

708
01:15:59,786 --> 01:16:02,716
For now, what is important for us...

709
01:16:03,053 --> 01:16:05,283
...is Alişar Bey.

710
01:16:07,050 --> 01:16:10,930
We'll triumph because of him.

711
01:16:18,302 --> 01:16:21,862
Dündar Bey, Alişar Bey wishes to see
you in the yard.

712
01:16:29,568 --> 01:16:30,388
This...

713
01:16:32,787 --> 01:16:35,847
This will be your last
crying, inshallah.

714
01:16:37,171 --> 01:16:40,181
They took our child but...

715
01:16:40,352 --> 01:16:43,252
...they won't take our home.

716
01:17:09,490 --> 01:17:12,720
How will you explain to my father that
you are working with the Mongols.

717
01:17:13,016 --> 01:17:15,636
Let's see what will he do when he
finds out.

718
01:17:16,968 --> 01:17:17,798
Aygül...

719
01:17:20,502 --> 01:17:25,572
I feel down in the mouth.
I can't take on with you.

720
01:17:25,620 --> 01:17:26,930
Get out of my sight!

721
01:17:26,960 --> 01:17:28,320
Mother, this can't be.

722
01:17:28,411 --> 01:17:32,781
Tell my father, he needs to know.

723
01:17:34,371 --> 01:17:36,071
Don't advise me, Aygül.

724
01:17:37,043 --> 01:17:40,263
You take care of yourself,
that's enough for me.

725
01:17:40,761 --> 01:17:43,481
We've seen what you did when
you knew a lot.

726
01:17:44,031 --> 01:17:48,031
My father will learn soon.
If not today, then tomorrow.

727
01:17:48,507 --> 01:17:50,367
If you don't tell him...

728
01:18:29,530 --> 01:18:31,460
What do you want from me, Turk?

729
01:18:31,582 --> 01:18:33,882
No need to be afraid, Princess Adelfa.

730
01:18:36,311 --> 01:18:38,831
I came to save you from being
a concubine to Geyhatu.

731
01:18:44,775 --> 01:18:46,435
I don't believe you.

732
01:18:47,404 --> 01:18:49,434
Calm down, Hatun.

733
01:18:53,811 --> 01:18:56,511
I didn't come here to hurt you.

734
01:18:56,612 --> 01:18:59,372
But to have you as a guest.

735
01:19:20,144 --> 01:19:21,834
What do you want from me?

736
01:19:26,099 --> 01:19:28,169
Preventing your marriage with Geyhatu.

737
01:20:01,260 --> 01:20:03,410
Are you ready for the big day, Dündar Bey?

738
01:20:04,040 --> 01:20:06,360
Till the unrest of Osman ends...

739
01:20:07,389 --> 01:20:11,889
...blood that will be spilled is halal
to me, Alişar Bey.

740
01:20:18,610 --> 01:20:22,610
Gündüz sieged everywhere with his alps,
Alişar Bey.

741
01:20:24,393 --> 01:20:26,623
It will be a hard battle.

742
01:20:28,770 --> 01:20:31,740
Before the sun sets, warriors
of Geyhatu...

743
01:20:32,220 --> 01:20:34,480
...will be under my command.

744
01:20:37,125 --> 01:20:40,220
We aren't alone.
Be at ease.

745
01:20:42,210 --> 01:20:45,470
You can't even imagine...

746
01:20:45,714 --> 01:20:47,954
...how much Geyhatu trusts me.

747
01:20:49,979 --> 01:20:51,159
Dündar Bey.

748
01:20:52,856 --> 01:20:56,656
The blood that will be spilled...

749
01:20:56,656 --> 01:20:59,956
...when your loyal alps and Beys
see you...

750
01:20:59,956 --> 01:21:03,956
...will be the end of the Osman calamity
that hurts your Tent like a plague.

751
01:21:03,986 --> 01:21:07,956
Alps on Söğüt and on patrol are on me.

752
01:21:09,693 --> 01:21:11,223
Don't worry.

753
01:21:15,275 --> 01:21:18,755
Those who crushed the succession
my brother gave to me...

754
01:21:19,130 --> 01:21:22,040
...will be crushed under my boots.

755
01:21:24,256 --> 01:21:28,256
It's the time of vengeance, Alişar Bey.

756
01:21:29,092 --> 01:21:32,742
I'll be in your debt for the
rest of my life.

757
01:21:32,809 --> 01:21:36,809
Not at all! I've done my duty
for these lands.

758
01:21:38,309 --> 01:21:40,859
I'm grateful to you.

759
01:21:41,800 --> 01:21:45,170
If it wasn't for a shrewd Bey like you...

760
01:21:45,320 --> 01:21:50,220
...there would be nothing left from the
Kayı Tent, other than good memories.

761
01:21:55,125 --> 01:21:57,235
And valiant people without graves...

762
01:21:59,628 --> 01:22:01,838
Your child, valiant Batur...

763
01:22:02,741 --> 01:22:07,071
...I wish he could be by your side
on this sacred day.

764
01:22:13,457 --> 01:22:16,557
I don't want Süleyman Şah's bloodline
to end with you...

765
01:22:18,793 --> 01:22:22,223
Zöhre Hatun can't give you another
child, anymore.

766
01:22:23,008 --> 01:22:27,848
But I'd like to find a Bey daughter
who will continue your bloodline.

767
01:22:30,734 --> 01:22:34,914
The one who will continue the bloodline
of my father Süleyman Şah...

768
01:22:34,975 --> 01:22:40,335
...is my son Bahadır, who I once exiled
because of Osman.

769
01:22:43,538 --> 01:22:45,068
Bahadır, you say?

770
01:22:49,089 --> 01:22:51,449
I learned that you have another child.

771
01:22:52,098 --> 01:22:53,988
That relieved me.

772
01:22:55,966 --> 01:22:59,966
May Allah look after your son.

773
01:23:21,859 --> 01:23:23,499
Why are you doing this?

774
01:23:24,136 --> 01:23:26,156
Mongols are our common enemy.

775
01:23:26,790 --> 01:23:27,910
Isn't it enough?

776
01:23:37,229 --> 01:23:39,529
I can't go back to Constaninople.

777
01:23:39,896 --> 01:23:42,836
We'll guest you at the Tent,
until things turn back to normal.

778
01:23:43,522 --> 01:23:46,042
Then, you can go anytime you want.

779
01:23:47,241 --> 01:23:49,581
I've been thinking of killing myself,
for days.

780
01:23:51,293 --> 01:23:54,853
How weird is that I'll survive with the
helping hand of the Turks I hate.

781
01:24:00,064 --> 01:24:01,064
Hatun...

782
01:24:06,256 --> 01:24:10,436
Don't bow down to anyone but the creator.

783
01:24:11,699 --> 01:24:13,459
May God protect you, Turk.

784
01:24:15,652 --> 01:24:17,772
I found tracks. They went this way!

785
01:24:19,561 --> 01:24:21,451
My Bey, I hear their voices.

786
01:24:21,464 --> 01:24:23,154
-Look everywhere!
- They are coming.

787
01:24:23,189 --> 01:24:25,219
Nobody knows we are here.

788
01:24:27,205 --> 01:24:28,005
Balgay...

789
01:24:31,632 --> 01:24:35,172
If we go together, we'll give them what
they want. They'll capture us.

790
01:24:35,943 --> 01:24:38,263
-Take the princess to the Tent.
-My Bey.

791
01:24:38,497 --> 01:24:39,687
Go.

792
01:24:40,116 --> 01:24:41,626
As you wish, my Bey.

793
01:24:46,585 --> 01:24:47,375
Come on.

794
01:24:54,474 --> 01:24:56,714
Balgay...
Come to me...

795
01:25:23,340 --> 01:25:25,840
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim...

796
01:25:44,653 --> 01:25:46,313
What's happening Akça?

797
01:25:47,372 --> 01:25:49,472
You look sorrowful.

798
01:25:50,490 --> 01:25:51,860
You look abstracted.

799
01:25:54,048 --> 01:25:56,038
I listen to my inner voice, Sheikh.

800
01:25:58,185 --> 01:26:00,735
We came here to wait for our Âhi brothers.

801
01:26:01,172 --> 01:26:03,562
Most of the friends at the Söğüt
are broken.

802
01:26:04,645 --> 01:26:06,725
We couldn't find a home.

803
01:26:09,152 --> 01:26:11,862
I know that despair doesn't fit your tent.

804
01:26:13,735 --> 01:26:16,115
But because of the trouble, we were
dealing with...

805
01:26:16,684 --> 01:26:18,654
...I'm very uncomfortable.

806
01:26:21,293 --> 01:26:25,293
On the 214th verse of Bakara,
Allah says...

807
01:26:28,981 --> 01:26:31,511
...Muslims, did you think that...

808
01:26:32,370 --> 01:26:34,390
...you can go to heaven before
experiencing...

809
01:26:34,934 --> 01:26:38,934
...the likes of things...

810
01:26:40,274 --> 01:26:42,964
...the ones before you experienced?

811
01:26:46,166 --> 01:26:48,096
Earth is the house of troubles...

812
01:26:48,781 --> 01:26:50,741
...and the grave of the living.

813
01:26:52,265 --> 01:26:56,545
The world is a place of trial, Akça.

814
01:26:58,411 --> 01:27:01,491
It takes patience...
It takes gratitude...

815
01:27:02,316 --> 01:27:04,556
It takes reasoning and resignation.

816
01:27:05,885 --> 01:27:09,285
In here, you will ask Allah's mercy...

817
01:27:10,466 --> 01:27:13,046
...so that you won't have to ask
it from people.

818
01:27:15,001 --> 01:27:18,261
This world is a delusion, Akça.

819
01:27:18,898 --> 01:27:23,168
As long as you don't forget the delusion,
you can't remember the truth.

820
01:27:25,331 --> 01:27:26,851
Where is the princess?

821
01:27:28,271 --> 01:27:31,881
I see that your power can
only match women.

822
01:27:33,120 --> 01:27:35,520
Come and fight me like a soldier.

823
01:27:36,859 --> 01:27:39,389
If you want to see a soldier...

824
01:27:41,368 --> 01:27:42,538
Come, Osman...

825
01:27:57,176 --> 01:27:58,096
Seize him.

826
01:28:19,051 --> 01:28:22,161
Comparing to what Muslims
lived trough in our prophet's time...

827
01:28:23,167 --> 01:28:25,337
...what trouble is ours?

828
01:28:27,130 --> 01:28:28,920
That discrimination...

829
01:28:28,920 --> 01:28:30,580
These years of grieving...

830
01:28:32,084 --> 01:28:36,854
After the emigration of Muslims
to Ethiopia...

831
01:28:37,498 --> 01:28:40,818
...polytheist had done everything
to Muslims.

832
01:28:41,628 --> 01:28:44,088
They stopped every kind of trade...

833
01:28:44,152 --> 01:28:46,492
...even marriages with them.

834
01:28:47,239 --> 01:28:49,969
This took three long years.

835
01:28:51,139 --> 01:28:54,349
Sufferings... Troubles... Poverty...

836
01:28:54,621 --> 01:28:57,761
Continued by growing even more,
day by day.

837
01:28:59,544 --> 01:29:04,344
Believers had to eat barks and leafs
to not starve...

838
01:29:05,115 --> 01:29:12,225
Cries of little children could be
heard from long distances.

839
01:29:13,683 --> 01:29:18,193
Just when they thought it was over,
other bad things happened.

840
01:29:20,733 --> 01:29:28,113
Our Prophet's uncle, Ebu Talib and
his wife Hadradth Hatice passed away.

841
01:29:30,369 --> 01:29:34,369
Just when they thought attacks
were over, it increased.

842
01:29:34,839 --> 01:29:36,179
Allah's messenger...

843
01:29:36,351 --> 01:29:40,061
...went to his relatives, to Tahif...

844
01:29:40,311 --> 01:29:44,311
...by taking his adopted child
Zeh bin Hares with him.

845
01:29:45,609 --> 01:29:49,819
But troubles found our master in there,
as well.

846
01:29:50,195 --> 01:29:52,475
First, they mocked him...

847
01:29:52,643 --> 01:29:55,603
...then, they stoned him.

848
01:29:56,742 --> 01:30:00,742
Even if the ones on the ground
had let it happen...

849
01:30:00,975 --> 01:30:04,975
...the ones on the sky did not.

850
01:30:06,129 --> 01:30:08,149
Angel Gabriel came down...

851
01:30:08,340 --> 01:30:12,340
..'' O' messenger of Allah, what do you
want me to do?''

852
01:30:14,251 --> 01:30:17,971
''Ask it, and I will crush these two
mountains on their heads'' he said.

853
01:30:19,607 --> 01:30:22,727
The prophet of mercy said no.

854
01:30:22,895 --> 01:30:23,625
No...

855
01:30:24,605 --> 01:30:28,605
''I want their generations to
have believers...

856
01:30:28,896 --> 01:30:32,896
who don't go against the words of Allah.''
he said.

857
01:30:34,795 --> 01:30:38,375
Oppression was more than words
could handle...

858
01:30:39,098 --> 01:30:41,678
...a word from Medina...

859
01:30:41,971 --> 01:30:44,111
...became a cure for wounds...

860
01:30:44,338 --> 01:30:46,338
...a relief for hearts.

861
01:30:48,125 --> 01:30:53,055
While polytheists were trying to finish
off Muslims with great effort in Mecca...

862
01:30:54,316 --> 01:30:58,256
The people at Medina were becoming
Muslim.

863
01:30:59,744 --> 01:31:03,744
They invited the Prophet of Mercy
to Medina.

864
01:31:05,366 --> 01:31:10,296
In a short time, there wasn't a house
that Islam hadn't entered.

865
01:31:11,272 --> 01:31:12,222
Then...

866
01:31:12,524 --> 01:31:17,224
Then, believers conquered Mecca.

867
01:31:22,588 --> 01:31:23,998
Summary is...

868
01:31:24,489 --> 01:31:26,909
The end of a night is a morning...

869
01:31:27,198 --> 01:31:29,128
...the end of winter is summer...

870
01:31:29,244 --> 01:31:32,614
...and the end of a slope is a flatness.

871
01:31:33,746 --> 01:31:36,206
Those who aren't patient to trouble...

872
01:31:36,206 --> 01:31:37,806
...can't reach happiness.

873
01:31:40,334 --> 01:31:41,944
Thank you, my Sheikh.

874
01:31:42,700 --> 01:31:43,730
Thank you.

875
01:32:50,096 --> 01:32:51,376
Aslı and Kerem.

876
01:32:52,891 --> 01:32:55,591
I've put a great effort.
It's finally over.

877
01:33:08,312 --> 01:33:11,512
I'll ask you for marriage
when my father comes back.

878
01:33:16,964 --> 01:33:23,514
My daughter, having a baby
isn't destined for you.

879
01:33:23,646 --> 01:33:28,256
I don't know if it ever will.

880
01:33:28,751 --> 01:33:31,692
Miracles are owned by Allah.

881
01:33:31,692 --> 01:33:35,589
Our Sare mother became a mother
when she was 90 years old...

882
01:33:35,589 --> 01:33:39,989
Maybe, a woman whose womb was
splintered can be a mother too.

883
01:33:44,291 --> 01:33:47,781
You always run away.

884
01:33:47,833 --> 01:33:51,512
You ignore me. It's not going to be
like that, Bala.

885
01:33:51,512 --> 01:33:55,911
Find another woman for yourself. I'm not
good for you.

886
01:33:55,911 --> 01:34:01,231
A child is a gift of Allah. A dagger
wound can't separate us when...

887
01:34:01,386 --> 01:34:05,816
we like each other that much.

888
01:34:06,835 --> 01:34:10,905
Osman, don't.

889
01:34:12,188 --> 01:34:17,288
I can't. You'll have kids.

890
01:34:18,476 --> 01:34:22,216
- I'm not good for you.
- Are you?

891
01:34:22,220 --> 01:34:26,310
Bala, I'm falling apart without you.

892
01:34:26,537 --> 01:34:30,867
Being without you is the biggest obstacle
between me and my tomorrow.

893
01:34:34,078 --> 01:34:38,050
You're the power, Bala.

894
01:34:38,050 --> 01:34:42,070
You're the strength and the
light of my way.

895
01:34:43,013 --> 01:34:49,150
You're my dream, my love.

896
01:34:51,950 --> 01:34:58,790
My biggest dream is to marry you after
receiving my Sheikh's consent.

897
01:35:03,458 --> 01:35:06,268
You're my love, Hatun.

898
01:35:09,638 --> 01:35:14,398
If Allah doesn't give us children...

899
01:35:17,361 --> 01:35:19,721
I'm fine with that.

900
01:35:20,119 --> 01:35:23,479
I'm fine with everything
when I'm with you.

901
01:35:25,904 --> 01:35:27,404
Tell me.

902
01:35:29,535 --> 01:35:32,095
Are you fine with that?

903
01:35:32,292 --> 01:35:38,292
I'm fine with everything
when I'm with you, Osman.

904
01:36:55,122 --> 01:37:02,612
I've waited much to kill you, Osman.

905
01:37:05,212 --> 01:37:08,812
The spirits are telling me that...

906
01:37:08,868 --> 01:37:13,818
"You wanted, we gave Osman to you."

907
01:37:17,358 --> 01:37:21,528
But Erlik han doesn't want your life.

908
01:37:22,045 --> 01:37:24,035
He wants your weapon.

909
01:37:24,157 --> 01:37:32,407
In this mighty way of Cengiz Han,
we are in the same way, Osman.

910
01:37:38,160 --> 01:37:40,090
Untie him.

911
01:37:52,667 --> 01:37:56,397
As I see, you don't want
Princess Adelfa....

912
01:37:56,418 --> 01:38:02,388
to marry Geyhatu.

913
01:38:02,730 --> 01:38:06,630
What do you want from me? I want to...

914
01:38:07,221 --> 01:38:11,531
fight with a brave man like you, Osman.

915
01:38:11,945 --> 01:38:14,455
I told you that my weapon isn't for sale!

916
01:38:14,455 --> 01:38:20,083
Sure I know I can't buy you by offering
post or gold.

917
01:38:20,083 --> 01:38:22,983
So why do you want my alliance?

918
01:38:24,905 --> 01:38:26,575
Give him.

919
01:38:41,819 --> 01:38:48,049
I would take your life if I wanted to,
Osman.

920
01:38:49,944 --> 01:38:55,216
You defeated me, and you are defeated
by Geyhatu.

921
01:38:55,216 --> 01:38:58,926
What do you mean?
Speak directly.

922
01:38:59,013 --> 01:39:06,193
Nobody knew where Princes Adelfa was going
except for Geyhatu and Byzantine Emperor.

923
01:39:06,537 --> 01:39:09,729
I see that you also knew.

924
01:39:09,729 --> 01:39:12,670
Somebody gave you that information.

925
01:39:12,670 --> 01:39:20,040
I don't know who did it, but I know why,
Osman.

926
01:39:21,969 --> 01:39:25,919
If Geyhatu had married Princess,

927
01:39:25,960 --> 01:39:28,703
it would end Turks.

928
01:39:28,703 --> 01:39:32,333
They gave you that information to
prevent this.

929
01:39:32,443 --> 01:39:39,743
I don't know who did it, Osman Bey.

930
01:39:40,096 --> 01:39:46,626
Only thing I know is we are in the same
path, Osman Bey.

931
01:39:46,626 --> 01:39:52,906
I prefer death to be with you.

932
01:39:52,910 --> 01:40:01,370
Would you? Even if Geyhatu sent a army
to your tent to destroy your brother?

933
01:40:46,140 --> 01:40:49,180
My condolences to you, Aygül Hatun.

934
01:40:49,293 --> 01:40:51,505
May he rest in peace.

935
01:40:51,505 --> 01:40:53,105
Amin.

936
01:40:53,749 --> 01:40:59,129
My brother is gone, but my father is here.
Thanks to you.

937
01:41:00,034 --> 01:41:03,224
May Allah be pleased with you.

938
01:41:14,020 --> 01:41:19,660
You have another trouble, Aygül Hatun.

939
01:41:20,234 --> 01:41:24,724
No.
Isn't that enough?

940
01:41:24,734 --> 01:41:31,584
Unfortunetaly, I heard you while I was
going to my room to take a book.

941
01:41:32,941 --> 01:41:37,781
I couldn't help but overhear what
Zöhre Hatun did.

942
01:41:38,203 --> 01:41:41,853
You are in a bad situation, I know.

943
01:41:42,282 --> 01:41:48,202
It's family issues. It would be better
if you hadn't heard, Alişar Bey.

944
01:41:52,929 --> 01:41:56,679
However you like, I didn't hear,
and you didn't speak.

945
01:41:57,075 --> 01:42:03,085
I didn't hear,
and you didn't speak.

946
01:42:04,460 --> 01:42:08,146
Even, you didn't know this.

947
01:42:08,146 --> 01:42:09,906
Why?

948
01:42:10,784 --> 01:42:13,804
My mother did wrong.

949
01:42:14,125 --> 01:42:19,795
My father needs to know.
How can I hide this?

950
01:42:20,832 --> 01:42:28,602
I am thinking, though. I don't know how
my father will react if I speak.

951
01:42:29,972 --> 01:42:31,962
I am afraid.

952
01:42:32,802 --> 01:42:39,702
Just wait.
Wait and see, Aygül Hatun.

953
01:42:41,355 --> 01:42:47,865
You need to think over the things
that will effect your life.

954
01:42:48,398 --> 01:42:51,948
You need to learn how to
ignore your feelings.

955
01:42:53,298 --> 01:42:56,481
Wait and see.

956
01:42:56,481 --> 01:42:59,881
- But...
- You were born as a daughter of Bey.

957
01:43:00,158 --> 01:43:04,098
And a bannerlord is in love with you.

958
01:43:07,914 --> 01:43:12,444
If Allah permits, and
you become my wife...

959
01:43:13,233 --> 01:43:16,683
You will be in a much bigger
policy.

960
01:43:16,726 --> 01:43:20,266
You'll have much more power.

961
01:43:20,768 --> 01:43:25,128
Don't do anything until you...

962
01:43:25,252 --> 01:43:27,632
have that power.

963
01:43:39,002 --> 01:43:42,012
Just let it be.

964
01:43:43,622 --> 01:43:49,312
And then, you can do whatever you want
to do.

965
01:44:09,191 --> 01:44:13,961
Also, anger doesn't looks good in you,
Aygül Hatun.

966
01:44:14,323 --> 01:44:19,513
You need to smile, flowers...

967
01:44:22,713 --> 01:44:25,293
and have jewelry.

968
01:44:32,445 --> 01:44:38,365
In my mansion, being happy is
connected with being silent.

969
01:44:41,016 --> 01:44:46,956
I know, what you want to tell your
father is important for you.

970
01:44:47,811 --> 01:44:52,081
But, it is not the right time.

971
01:45:04,412 --> 01:45:07,692
I accept your gift, Alişar Bey.

972
01:45:35,252 --> 01:45:37,372
I am listening.

973
01:45:38,190 --> 01:45:41,580
Dündar Bey is still alive.

974
01:45:44,181 --> 01:45:50,501
-How do you know?
-I've spies in Söğüt and Konya, Osman Bey.

975
01:45:51,945 --> 01:45:56,755
Geyhatu wants Cengiz Han's laws
and his dagger.

976
01:45:56,769 --> 01:45:59,094
Just like you.

977
01:45:59,094 --> 01:46:04,894
You hate me, but you know I can
face you in war, like a man

978
01:46:07,633 --> 01:46:12,303
However, Geyhatu isn't like me.
He tricked both of us.

979
01:46:12,511 --> 01:46:18,571
Alişar turned out to be Geyhatu's spy.

980
01:46:20,002 --> 01:46:22,432
What do you mean?

981
01:46:22,519 --> 01:46:30,309
Geyhatu gave Alişar bannerlordship.

982
01:46:31,258 --> 01:46:36,138
A huge army is going to Söğüt tonight.

983
01:46:36,850 --> 01:46:43,440
Cengiz Han's laws is only thing he wants.

984
01:46:43,911 --> 01:46:47,771
Wait, don't get angry now.

985
01:46:47,792 --> 01:46:51,002
I didn't finish.

986
01:46:51,347 --> 01:46:54,747
Do you know where Dündar Bey is now?

987
01:46:56,150 --> 01:46:58,630
In Alişar's hand.

988
01:47:02,739 --> 01:47:07,949
He want to destroy my brother and get
Dündar in the lead.

989
01:47:10,469 --> 01:47:15,389
It was him who shot my uncle
while we were fighting.

990
01:47:16,298 --> 01:47:19,018
Your uncle.

991
01:47:19,827 --> 01:47:22,317
and Batur.

992
01:48:11,011 --> 01:48:14,911
Gündüz Bey, Alişar Bey invited you to
the mansion.

993
01:48:16,886 --> 01:48:19,986
Give him my blessings, Zorba.

994
01:48:20,947 --> 01:48:25,507
Accepting the invitation is sunnah.
I will come before it gets dark.

995
01:48:26,658 --> 01:48:29,018
Eyvallah (okay) my Bey.

996
01:48:38,244 --> 01:48:43,404
If you go, they will kill you, son.

997
01:48:43,980 --> 01:48:46,210
I know, Bamsı Bey.

998
01:48:46,459 --> 01:48:49,309
So, you are not going, ha?

999
01:48:53,347 --> 01:48:57,777
You gave me that advice in the
Alp class, Bamsı Bey.

1000
01:48:59,039 --> 01:49:02,509
"If you don't face the trouble,
it gets bigger...

1001
01:49:02,538 --> 01:49:05,228
you need to face it...

1002
01:49:05,424 --> 01:49:10,294
- Either it takes you down, or you do.
- Either it takes you down, or you do.

1003
01:49:13,760 --> 01:49:18,770
Eyvallah, son.
Than it is time to fight.

1004
01:49:19,483 --> 01:49:22,503
Listen to me, Bamsı Bey.

1005
01:49:23,945 --> 01:49:26,815
Thank Allah, you are better, my Bey.

1006
01:49:26,939 --> 01:49:31,799
I will get better to take revenge for
my son, Saltug.

1007
01:49:32,568 --> 01:49:35,358
Revenge is for valiants.

1008
01:49:36,441 --> 01:49:38,991
Today, we take revenge.

1009
01:49:40,287 --> 01:49:41,737
Aygül.

1010
01:49:42,611 --> 01:49:46,751
My father needs to know what you did.

1011
01:49:50,544 --> 01:49:53,024
Is there any news about Osman?

1012
01:49:53,182 --> 01:49:59,132
No. However, inshallah he will see
you in the charge when he comes.

1013
01:49:59,132 --> 01:50:03,502
I can't be sure about anything before
Osman dies, Saltug.

1014
01:50:03,597 --> 01:50:07,827
I know, my Bey, I know.
It's Osman's end.

1015
01:50:07,908 --> 01:50:13,068
Geyhatu sent a huge army.
They will be here before it gets dark.

1016
01:50:13,814 --> 01:50:18,174
Alişar Bey sent Zorba to Gündüz.

1017
01:50:18,363 --> 01:50:20,633
He invited him to his mansion.

1018
01:50:20,689 --> 01:50:26,759
When Gündüz comes, he will be
punsihed, and the tribe will be mine.

1019
01:50:29,577 --> 01:50:32,512
Today, we call acount, Saltug.

1020
01:50:32,512 --> 01:50:35,882
No one could stop it.

1021
01:50:39,987 --> 01:50:42,957
Father, I have something to tell you.

1022
01:50:46,954 --> 01:50:53,064
Geyhatu wanted to impose a tax on Byzantine
and get gold with this marriage.

1023
01:50:53,782 --> 01:50:58,352
And you wanted to destroy Byzantine
and get gold...

1024
01:50:59,368 --> 01:51:02,208
with Cengiz Han's laws' power.

1025
01:51:02,406 --> 01:51:08,176
Cengiz Han says: there is only one
power that unites two opponents.

1026
01:51:09,237 --> 01:51:11,477
The benefit.

1027
01:51:17,011 --> 01:51:20,071
Where your Alp take Princess to?

1028
01:51:24,121 --> 01:51:26,241
Somewhere secure.

1029
01:51:30,843 --> 01:51:36,253
Are you looking for trouble by keeping
that woman alive, Osman?

1030
01:51:36,285 --> 01:51:40,175
Mercy is no good, don't you know?

1031
01:51:41,084 --> 01:51:43,494
What about Alişar?

1032
01:51:46,080 --> 01:51:51,250
His friendship with Sofia,
His interest in trading,

1033
01:51:51,638 --> 01:51:54,598
Geyhatu wanted these.

1034
01:51:57,167 --> 01:52:01,687
Until I came and send Alişar to Konya.

1035
01:52:03,495 --> 01:52:06,155
Damn that day I sent him!

1036
01:52:06,281 --> 01:52:09,351
I sent him to Konya instead of killing
him!

1037
01:52:10,739 --> 01:52:13,759
That was the most stupid thing I have
ever done.

1038
01:52:15,745 --> 01:52:20,205
My uncle thinks I killed Batur.

1039
01:52:20,932 --> 01:52:27,772
That's why they will kill first Gündüz,
then Samsa Bey and Bamsı Bey.

1040
01:52:30,081 --> 01:52:33,641
At the end, you.

1041
01:52:37,277 --> 01:52:42,917
Your sword is ready, your
horse is ready.

1042
01:52:43,241 --> 01:52:45,851
If you want to, go to your tent.

1043
01:52:47,168 --> 01:52:55,928
But, when you go, you'll see Gündüz,
Bamsı Bey and Samsa Bey are dead.

1044
01:52:56,676 --> 01:53:04,726
You'll see Alişar as the bannerlord and
Dündar Bey in your father's throne.

1045
01:53:06,708 --> 01:53:13,688
Or, we both take what we deserve and
go on.

1046
01:53:14,750 --> 01:53:23,400
Either be with me and fight Geyhatu, Alişar,
Dündar.

1047
01:53:27,078 --> 01:53:30,598
Or go to your tent and die.

1048
01:53:36,312 --> 01:53:38,952
Your choice, Osman.

1049
01:53:53,145 --> 01:53:55,075
It's a deal, Balgay.

1050
01:53:58,970 --> 01:54:01,270
I am with you.

1051
01:54:04,473 --> 01:54:07,443
May our alliance be good.

1052
